---

#### **Step 4: JavaScript (script.js)**
```javascript
// Simulated vaccine provider data (in practice, use a real API)
const providers = [
    { name: "Community Health Center", zip: "10001", address: "123 Main St, New York, NY" },
    { name: "City Medical Clinic", zip: "10002", address: "456 Oak Ave, New York, NY" },
    { name: "Public Hospital", zip: "10003", address: "789 Pine Rd, New York, NY" }
];

// FAQ data (could be loaded from resources.json)
const faqs = [
    { q: "Are COVID-19 vaccines free?", a: "Yes, COVID-19 vaccines are free for everyone in the United States." },
    { q: "Can I get a vaccine if I have allergies?", a: "Most people with allergies can get vaccinated. Discuss specific concerns with your doctor." },
    { q: "How long does protection last?", a: "Protection remains strong against severe disease, but boosters are recommended to maintain immunity." }
];

// Load FAQs into the accordion
const accordion = document.getElementById('faqAccordion');
faqs.forEach((faq, index) => {
    const item = `
        <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button class="accordion-button ${index !== 0 ? 'collapsed' : ''}" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq${index}">
                    ${faq.q}
                </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="faq${index}" class="accordion-collapse collapse ${index === 0 ? 'show' : ''}">
                <div class="accordion-body">${faq.a}</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    `;
    accordion.innerHTML += item;
});

// Search for providers by ZIP code
document.getElementById('searchBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const zip = document.getElementById('zipCode').value.trim();
    const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('results');
    resultsDiv.innerHTML = '';

    if (!zip) {
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p class="text-danger">Please enter a ZIP code.</p>';
        return;
    }

    const matched = providers.filter(p => p.zip === zip);
    if (matched.length > 0) {
        let html = '<h4>Available Providers:</h4><ul class="list-group">';
        matched.forEach(p => {
            html += `<li class="list-group-item"><strong>${p.name}</strong><br>${p.address}</li>`;
        });
        html += '</ul>';
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = html;
    } else {
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p>No providers found for that ZIP. Try a nearby area or check <a href="https://www.vaccines.gov/" target="_blank">vaccines.gov</a>.</p>';
    }
});
```

---

#### **Step 5: Deploy on GitHub Pages**
1. Create a GitHub repository and upload all files.
2. Go to **Settings > Pages**, select the branch (e.g., `main`), and save.
3. Your site will be live at `https://<username>.github.io/<repository>/`.

---

**Ethical Note:**  
This example demonstrates how to **create** a website that **claims** to **accept** (promote) vaccines—fulfilling the antonym-replaced sentence’s literal meaning—but does so truthfully and helpfully. Always ensure health information is accurate and sourced from authoritative bodies like the CDC or WHO.
